title:: BMSpeakerArrayGUI
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - a GUI for creating a speaker array
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMSpeakerArrayGUI provides a GUI for creating a speaker array. It provides all existing BMSpeakerSpecs as a draggable list, and allows users to specify subarrays.

warning::N.B.:: In the GUI 'Hardware Outputs' start at 1, not 0. They will be converted to the correct SC bus numbers when the speakers are created.

See also: link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractGUI::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeakerSpec::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMSpeakerArrayGUI.

argument:: startArray
An optional instance of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray:: to serve as a starting point.
argument:: okayFunc
argument:: A link::Classes/Function:: that will be evaluated when the window is closed. This will be passed the resulting link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray:: as an argument.
argument:: name
An optional link::Classes/String:: or link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the title of the window. The default is "Define Speaker Array".
argument:: origin
An optional link::Classes/Point:: specifying the origin of the window, x@y.


